nce that  out i mean how do we look after the uk  look after our citizens while also  standing up to our responsibility  to the international community in third  world countries  yeah he's a great question look first of  all we've got  355 million doses secured  and we've got seven different suppliers  coming down the track  subject to the regulatory approval so  we've got quite a diverse supply chain  because i know  that's something people have been asked  because of course our first duty our  first priority is to make sure  the british people are as safe and  protected as possible but you're  absolutely right that we're only as safe  as the weakest link in this global chain  it's a global  pandemic and we need global solutions  and we feel a great sense of duty and  moral responsibility but also  british interest in making sure uh  poorer people around the world  vulnerable countries get the vaccine  that's why this prime minister  led the gabi vaccine summit and raised  smashed the target raising 8.8 billion  dollars  for that equitable international  distribution that's why we've been a  leader on kovacs  which is the mechanism to allow poorer  countries access to that  vaccine we're a world leader in this um  and  so yes whether whether it's the the  research that we're seeing at oxford and  imperial  whether it's getting uh the roll out of  the vaccines which we've managed to do  this  this uh this week uh right the way  through to the international  leadership that we're providing we're  making sure that we  are not just looking at our secretary  the british people but also  the rest of the world very good to talk  to you this morning

